Id: ssh029i
Severity: INFO
Category: ssh
Check: check_ssh
Fix: Set FingerprintHash sha256 (the default).
References: sshd_config(5); ssh-keygen(1)
Controls: CIS 4.1, 5.4; NIST AC-17, IA-2; ISO 8.5, 8.20; CE Secure configuration, User access control

FingerprintHash is md5: the key fingerprints sshd writes to its log
(with LogLevel VERBOSE, the fingerprint of the key each login used) are
MD5, which an attacker can produce collisions for and which the other
tools (ssh-keygen -l, the client's known_hosts prompts) stopped using
in OpenSSH 6.8. A log of MD5 fingerprints is harder to match against
today's SHA256 ones when working out who logged in. The default is
sha256.
